INTRO(1)

NAME
     intro - introduction to AZ/UX

DESCRIPTION
     AZ/UX is a small UNIX-like operating system for the az030, a 68030
     computer with a 68882 FPU, SCSI disks and a serial console. It
     provides processes with protected address spaces, a hierarchical
     file system, pipes, signals, job control, users and permissions.

   Logging in
     Log in as root (no password on a fresh system) or as user. Set
     passwords with passwd(1). The shell, sh(1), reads /etc/profile and
     ~/.profile; type help for its built-in commands.

   Finding your way around
     ls /bin                 the programs
     man -l                  every manual page
     man -k word             pages about a word
     man sh, man edit        the shell and the text editor

   Files
     /bin, /sbin             programs (/sbin: system administration)
     /etc                    configuration: passwd, group, shadow, rc,
                             profile, motd, issue, hostname
     /usr/include            C header files
     /usr/lib                libc.a and crt0.o
     /usr/src                sources: libc and examples
     /usr/share/man          these manual pages
     /tmp                    temporary files (cleared at boot)
     /home                   home directories
     /dev                    devices: console, tty, null, zero, random,
                             sd0-sd6 (SCSI disks)

   Programming
     cc(1) compiles C, as(1) assembles 68030 code, ld(1) links and
     make(1) drives builds. edit(1) is a screen editor. Start with the
     examples in /usr/src/examples:

         cd /tmp
         cc -o hello /usr/src/examples/hello.c
         ./hello

   Shutting down
     Run halt, reboot or poweroff as root. Data is written to disk
     every few seconds and by sync(1).

SEE ALSO
     sh(1), edit(1), cc(1), make(1), man(1), intro(2), intro(3)
